From: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm: sdp: make legacy bootlogo memory metadata optional

The atomic scanout path uses the address of its GEM-DMA framebuffer; it does
not allocate from or map /sdp_mmap/samsung,gfx0.  Do not prevent DRM probe
when that legacy boot-logo metadata is absent or incomplete.  Keep parsing it
as diagnostic information when it is available.

This does not prove CMA, DMA-BUF import, or a Panfrost allocation is valid for
scanout.  The existing 32-bit DMA mask and plane address validation remain the
only implemented scanout contract.  No hardware values change, the DT node
remains disabled, and no hardware test was performed.

Signed-off-by: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sdp/sdp_drm.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sdp/sdp_drm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sdp/sdp_drm.c
index 6029053e8072..0ba92d5a8d56 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sdp/sdp_drm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sdp/sdp_drm.c
@@ -486,7 +486,6 @@ static int sdp_drm_parse_gfx_mem(struct device *dev, u32 *addr, u32 *size)
 	np = of_find_node_by_name(NULL, "sdp_mmap");
 	if (!np) {
-		dev_err(dev, "sdp_mmap node not found in device tree\n");
-		return -ENODEV;
+		return 0;
 	}
 
 	ret = of_property_read_u32_array(np, "samsung,gfx0", data, 3);
@@ -494,6 +493,6 @@ static int sdp_drm_parse_gfx_mem(struct device *dev, u32 *addr, u32 *size)
 	of_node_put(np);
 	if (ret) {
-		dev_err(dev, "samsung,gfx0 not found in sdp_mmap: %d\n", ret);
-		return ret;
+		dev_dbg(dev, "samsung,gfx0 unavailable: %d\n", ret);
+		return 0;
 	}
 
 	*addr = data[1];
-- 
